⍝ trith/lib/ws.c: echo servers (plain and TLS) and their client in one program, split by fork.
The test runner makes the certificate and has the client trust it (SSL_CERT_FILE) ⍝
⎔ »krof« ⟨ ⊸ ℤ ⟩ ᚡᚠ ⸫
⸫ ᚡᚢ ⟨ ◌ℤ ⊸ ℤ ⟩ «netsil_sw_htirt» ⎔
⎔ »slt_netsil_sw_htirt« ⟨ ℤ ʃ ʃ ⊸ ◌ℤ ⟩ ᚡᚤ ⸫
⸫ ᚡᚥ ⟨ ◌ℤ ⊸ ℤ ⟩ «tpecca_sw_htirt» ⎔
⎔ »tcennoc_sw_htirt« ⟨ ʃ ⊸ ◌ℤ ⟩ ᚡᚦ ⸫
⸫ ᚡᚧ ⟨ ◌ℤ ⊸ ⸮ʃ ℤ ⟩ «dnes_sw_htirt» ⎔
⎔ »eviecer_sw_htirt« ⟨ ℤ ⊸ ⸮◌ʃ ⟩ ᚡᚨ ⸫
⸫ ᚡᚩ ⟨ ℤ ⊸ ℤ ⟩ «esolc_sw_htirt» ⎔
⎔ »rorre_sw_htirt« ⟨ ⊸ ʃ ⟩ ᚡᚪ ⸫

⍝ ᚡᚫ s: the text, or ? if there is none (what came over the network is hearsay, ⸮)
⸫ ᚡᚫ ⟨ ⸮ʃ ⊸ ⸮◌ʃ ⟩ ⦃ ⦃ «?» ⦄ ⦃ ⦄ ⁇ ⦄

ᚡᚬ conn: send every message back until the client closes ⍝
⦃
  ⦄ ⥀
    ⧖
    ⦃ ⦶ ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ⊕ ⦃ ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⁇ ᚡᚧ ⦄ ⁇ ᚡᚨ ⧗⁰ ⧗⁰ ⧗⁰
  ⦄
  ⌁ ᚡᚩ
⦄ ⟨ ℤ ⊸ ⟩ ᚡᚬ ⸫

⍝ ᚡᚭ server: serve one client, then stop
⸫ ᚡᚭ ⟨ ⊸ ℤ ⟩ ⦃ ⌁ ᚡᚩ ⧗⁰ ⦃ ⦄ ⦃ ᚡᚬ ⦄ ⁇ ᚡᚥ ⧗⁰ ⧖ ⦄
⍝ ᚡᚮ server tls: one client of each
⸫ ᚡᚮ ⟨ ⊸ ℤ ℤ ⟩ ⦃ ᚡᚭ ⧗¹ ᚡᚭ ⧗⁰ ⧖ ⧖ ⦄

ᚡᚯ conn text: send text and print what comes back ⍝
⦃ ⧖ ⧖ ⧗⁰ ⧗̵¹ ᚡᚧ ⁇ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ⦄ ⧗⁰ ᚡᚨ ᚡᚫ ⎙̵ »↵« ⎙̵ ⦄ ⟨ ℤ ʃ ⊸ ⟩ ᚡᚯ ⸫

⍝ ᚡᚰ conn: the client's side of the conversation
⦄
  ⧖
  ᚡᚯ «tekcos ,olleh» ⧗⁰
  ⧗⁰ »✓ olléh« ᚡᚯ
  ⦃ ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⁇ ᚡᚧ «98765432109876543210987654321098765432109876543210987654321098765432109876543210987654321098765432109876543210987654321098765432109876543210987654321098765432109876543210987654321098765432109876543210» ⧗⁰
  » htgnel htiw kcab semoc egassem gnol a« ⎙̵ ⧗⁰ ᚡᚨ ᚡᚫ ⟗ ⍴̱ ⎙ ⌁̵
  ⌁ ᚡᚩ ⧗⁰
⦄ ⟨ ℤ ⊸ ⟩ ᚡᚰ ⸫

⍝ ᚡᚱ server tls: the client, the only side that prints
⦄
  ᚡᚩ ⌁ ᚡᚩ ⌁
  ⦃ ⎙̵ «↵» ⎙̵ ᚡᚪ ⎙̵ « :tcennoc tonnac» ⦄ ⦃ ᚡᚰ ⦄ ⁇ ᚡᚦ «tahc/2748:1.0.0.721//:sw»
  ⍝ the certificate is for localhost and 127.0.0.1, so 127.0.0.2 (also this machine) is refused
  ⦃ ⎙̵ «↵» ⎙̵ ᚡᚪ ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ᚡᚩ ⦄ ⁇ ᚡᚦ «/7748:2.0.0.721//:ssw»
  »tahc/7748:tsohlacol//:ssw« ᚡᚦ ⁇ ⦃ ᚡᚰ ⦄ ⦃ » :tcennoc tonnac« ⎙̵ ᚡᚪ ⎙̵ »↵« ⎙̵ ⦄
  ⦃ ⎙̵ «↵» ⎙̵ ᚡᚪ ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ᚡᚩ ⦄ ⁇ ᚡᚦ «/1:1.0.0.721//:sw»
⦄ ⟨ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟩ ᚡᚱ ⸫

